## Growth triggers — run `make audit` before the quarter ends when…

The twelve-point CI-integrity audit runs on a quarterly schedule (`.github/workflows/audit.yml`
opens an issue). Run it early, by hand, when any of these happens — each one changes what the
checks have to cover:

- CI time per pull request crosses ~15 minutes.
- The codebase doubles.
- A new service or language is added.
- A new automation account or AI agent gets write access.
- You approach your first paying customer.{% if solo_maintainer %}
  Before that point: a separate machine account for the agent (write, not admin), and re-run
  `copier update --data solo_maintainer=false` so the forge, not local agent settings, keeps
  the agent and the owner apart. Today both act through one account (see ONBOARDING.md §2).{% endif %}

